gic in the final  years of the war this easily explains  why other countries were unaware but if  we turn our attention to those  governments domestic issues we can find  even more reasons  as you might have imagined almost every  government had its own mughal government  and then a separate corresponding  magical government with places like the  uk and the us these dual governments are  pretty easy to see  since we've encountered them in film and  books  there are over 190 muggle countries in  the world but actually in the wizarding  community  some of the magical governments don't  keep the same borders as their muggle  counterparts  in regards to their magical government  some countries actually have entirely  different borders which makes sense  after centuries of warfare  european countries gained and lost  territory fairly often which was  something their local wizarding  communities often chose to ignore  the changing borders of their muggle  nation states were only an annoyance for  the wizards who were content to keep  their traditional holdings which means  there might have been even more magical  ministries than muggle congresses  now you might be wondering what does  that have to do with voldemort well as  you can see there were over a hundred  other wizarding governments and they had  their own domestic issues to deal with  there were likely many other pressing  matters within each and every country  that made up the international  confederation of wizards and maybe just  like voldemort's campaign against the  british ministry of magic many other  countries might have been facing their  own civil wars  even if they had heard the whispers of  voldemort's return  they simply didn't have the power to  investigate it further  voldemort wasn't an international threat  even though lord voldemort was a  terrible threat to the british ministry  of magic he might not have been a worthy  opponent for other countries  even during the first wizarding war when  voldemort led his campaigns against  british wizards and witches the  international confederation of wizards  didn't form any meaningful position  against him  as the wizarding world's version of the  united nations the international  confederation of wizards largest  contribution to the wizarding world was  to keep their people safe  for most of recorded history that meant  creating and agreeing to laws that kept  their true powers hidden from the mughal  populace  but just like the united nations the  international confederation of wizards  also was responsible for resolving  disputes between its member states  so if voldemort were to assume power in  britain and then turn his attention  towards other countries to conquer  it would fall to the international  confederation of wizards to stop him  but according to the few records we have  the international organization never  even convened a committee in order to  discuss a concerted defense strategy  in case voldemort crossed the english  channel it was a domestic affair if you  close your eyes spin a globe and  randomly point your finger to country  you'd have a nine percent chance of  landing on one that is currently  fighting in a civil war  and even though we don't have a complete  list of historical records from the  international wizarding world  it's not hard to imagine that civil wars  and internal strife were all too common  amongst wizards and witches as well  when it comes to muggles many countries  often took a non-interventionist  approach  even though civil wars and strife led to  inconceivable suffering and bloodshed  most civil wars were allowed to proceed  without interference from neighboring  states and the reason was simple  trying to help only made matters worse  worse for the neighboring states and  often worse for the country that was  plunged into the civil war  and that non-interventionist philosophy  was even stronger amongst wizarding  governments the magical congress of the  united states was one of the most  isolationist regimes in the entire world  but its values were shared amongst most  others they simply wanted to protect  their own people from muggle persecution  and didn't want to risk their safety by  openly supporting or challenging warring  parties halfway around the world  hope it didn't spread appeasement if  international wizarding communities  didn't intervene in britain because they  thought it wasn't any of their business  then they must have hoped for one thing  that voldemort's greed didn't extend to  their country  if they were able to appease voldemort  and his death eaters then the  international wizarding community might  be able to avoid open wall which was  always what they feared the most  war between wizards was catastrophic it  was not only tragic for the amount of  lives lost in the conflicts but it also  presented a unique challenge the open  conflict threatened to reveal the  wizarding world to mughals  perhaps foreign governments like the  minister deserve magic de la france and  the magical congress of the united  states of america knew of voldemort's  return and had agreed to not intervene  if the dark lord kept his sights on only  britain  without any proof it's hard to guess at  how likely this policy of appeasement  was  even if there was no formal conferences  between death eaters and foreign  delegations they must have had some sort  of contact with each other  although wizarding governments didn't  like to intervene in the affairs of  others they still needed to keep a close  eye on international events and  voldemort's second rise was certainly  something to watch  they supported voldemort there's one  potential reason that we've yet to  mention and it might be the most  controversial  other countries might have actually  supported voldemort's position  when we look back at the history of the  wizarding community in britain we'll  find a strange tradition  although many of their constituents  prided themselves on being purebloods  the leaders of the wizarding world  actually didn't care that much about  heritage  during the founding of hogwarts school  of witchcraft and wizardry all four  founders initially agreed to let half  bloods and muggleborns enroll in their  school  in fact when salazar therein later  changed his mind and wanted to ban all  but pure bloods from attending the other  three founders refused to consent as you  can see from some of its earliest  history the british wizarding world was  fairly progressive  at least compared to surrounding nations  since we know so much about the history  of wizards and witches in england  calling the british magical community  progressive might sound strange  especially considering their treatment  of goblins but when we extend our look  to the more ethnically homogenous  countries in central europe the middle  east and asia  their policies were far more  conservative and voldemort's position  might not have actually been so  unconventional if we just look at the  mughal government of japan we can find  numerous examples of the hardships that  non-ethnic japanese citizens face and  interestingly treating citizens of  varying ethnicities with equal rights  isn't a great priority or even legally  protected if we apply that same sense of  ethno-national pride to the wizarding  community then the students and  graduates of mahutu koro the wizarding  school of japan might not actually see  the big fuss about voldemort  to them and many other countries around  the world pure blood supremacy might  have been normal  conclusion  in the end we might never know the real  reason that the international wizarding  community failed to help harry potter  and his allies  for my money i'd bet it's an equal mix  of all of these theories many of the  countries might not have seen what the  big fuss was about and others might have  simply not wanted to involve themselves  in a civil war add to that voldemort's  expert coup of the ministry of magic and  foreign ministries could have claimed  ignorance to voldemort's rise  even though they could probably tell  that something was amiss  and that's it for this video what do you  think leave a comment down below until  next time remember it does not do to  dwell on dreams and forget to live  [Music]  [Music]  you

